{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/71491-non-human-hunters","id":71491,"title":"Non-human hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-13T12:02:03-08:00","id":71491,"title":"Non-human hunters","content":"One of the books makes a super quick mention that Cheiron will, occasionally, hire vampires, werewolves, mages, etc. It also suggests that these employees may have been implanted with Thaumatechnology. Anyone done anything with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:42:50-08:00","id":71529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/71491-non-human-hunters#post71491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the books makes a super quick mention that Cheiron will, occasionally, hire vampires, werewolves, mages, etc. It also suggests that these employees may have been implanted with Thaumatechnology. Anyone done anything with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly, Cheiron gives brief outline that it likes Vampires both as investors and resources but other than that, it doesn't seem to give much. Werewolves are viewed as resources worth much more being cut up on the table and Mages are a collective &quot;meh&quot; due to lack of biological stuff that can be harvested and don't seem to want to use them as harvesters due to them being kinda clued in on the Awakened and know how nosy those guys get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:03:33-08:00","id":71643,"title":"","content":"I've been itching to play as a Ghoul who works for Cheiron. They have him on the leash with a steady supply of blood (and a tasty paycheck), while he's one of the better field agents and brings in a fair amount of profit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T20:44:20-08:00","id":71803,"title":"","content":"Not with Cheiron, but before we moved into Blood and Smoke rules the players were playing a mix of ghouls and Hunters. Aegis Kai Doru and Ashwood Abbey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T15:49:47-08:00","id":72283,"title":"","content":"In my Chronicle, TFV has what is called the &quot;Green Book&quot;, which is a database regrouping all the ENE the conspiracy considers assets, whether as an occasional informant or an auxilary. The last word designates the para-human ENE (mages, vampires, werewolves ...) who Valkyrie trusts enough to go on TFV missions, with a Hunter cell or alone (only for the most trustworthy).<br /> As ENE, these people can't be full TFV members (a safety measure against direct infiltration by ENE organisations), but the conspiracy has other ways to retribute their help, money of course, but also things like tolerance of their deeds (up to a limit) by the local TFV, amnesia of criminal records, immunity against certain offenses during missions, federal made identities, infos from federal databases ... For the most usefull auxilaries, it can go up to armed squad backup (if the ENE signals a serious danger to the United States or a major criminal operation with heavy supernatural elements), restricted direct access to Valkyrie files or storehouses (under an agent's supervision), near immunity to the actions of Valkyrie agents (in fact, once an ENE has reached such an high level of usefulness, an agent would need real serious proves of federal crimes before killing him, or he would be in trouble) and offers to take Black Book assignments (in exchange for a big help later).<br /> One thing to consider for the type of things an auxilary can ask and its place in the Green Book is the reason why he does work for TFV in the first place: one who perform his tasks because the agency has dirt on him will be placed lower than one who does so out of altruism or patriotism (the conspiracy knows that while the latter feeling is less pronounced in the ENE population in general, it knows it exists and prizes ENE who help for this reason).<br /> By the way, some of the higher ups who also know about TFV vampire backers consider such ENE safer assets (as they do actual field jobs and lack ways to seriously harm the agency) than the &quot;leeches&quot;, and an indirect way to strike back at their blood-drinking financers if they decide to go overboard. A few top agents trust a long known auxilary as a trusted friend, beyond what would be normally considered acceptable.<br /> Of course, the full Green Book is opened only to the highest echelons of the conspiracy, but mid/upper-mid agents have access to the files about the Green ENE in their area of operation. Operatives lower in the hierarchy only hear of such ENE on a need-to-know basis, whether because their superiors signaled the ENE to them, or vice-versa.<br /> Finally, it must be known that an ENE entry in the Green Book contains its name, eventual aliases, address, type (Mage, Werewolf...), known skills (both mundane and supernatural), acquaintances, psy evaluation, a list of missions accomplished (with links to the mission reports), suggestions on which types of mission it should or should not be assigned to (i.e: the line the ENE will not cross; the conspiracy likes ENE ready to do much for America, but not psychopaths), and a list of tactics to be used in case the supernatural being becomes a danger and has to be terminated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/8.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":305,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/305-kergonan","user":"Kergonan","date":". 02-15-2014, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/305-kergonan","name":"Kergonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T08:19:12-08:00","id":73725,"title":"","content":"Not using the Cheiron group myself either, but my current hunter game just turned into Tier 3 as the group joined an organisation similar to TF:V. In addition to the humans the group also consists of a Fetch a half-angel (although he's mostly human, about as angelic as one of the Lucifuge is demonic). Works nicely so far, although there may still be some fallout since the Fetch hasn't revealed her true self to the others yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/586-gurrgel","name":"Gurrgel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}